This is a MATE panel applet to control any media player compatible with mpris2.

Requires:
 * MATE panel (GTK3, libmate-panel-applet)
 * playerctl: https://github.com/altdesktop/playerctl
 * libsoup3: to download the album art published by remote players

The applet shows previous, play/pause, stop and next buttons and binds
to the first player detected on the session bus.

The popup menu of the applet shows:

 * "Now Playing": the artist and title of the current track of the
   selected player, with its album art when enabled.
 * "Players": a radio list with every player detected on the bus that
   allows switching the player to control.

The preferences dialog offers three switches (disabled by default):

 * Show what is playing on other players: list the current track of
   every detected player in the selection submenu.
 * Show album art for the current player: display the album art of the
   current track in the "Now Playing" entry.
 * Show album art for the other players: display the album art of each
   player in the selection submenu.

The album art is read from the "mpris:artUrl" metadata published by
the players. Local files are loaded directly, and remote artwork is
downloaded with libsoup and cached under $XDG_CACHE_HOME/
mate-multimedia-control/, so it is only downloaded once.
